{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101377","id":2779080539,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc6lpWdb","number":101377,"title":"Mesh normals have sudden pops when using non-orthonormal basis","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2025-01-10T01:36:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T15:25:20Z","closed_at":"2026-06-18T15:25:20Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.3.stable and 4.4.dev7\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a mesh has a non-orthonormal basis (e.g. non-uniform scale or skewed transform), its normals experience sudden \"pops\" / changes at certain thresholds. I'm not sure what these thresholds actually are. For example while you are adjusting only the Z component of the scale, or if you are skewing the mesh, then at some point, the normals will suddenly change from one version to another.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/50220acc-13a8-491e-b48b-aeccdb0e3c01)\n\nThe expected behaviour is for the normals to be adjusted smoothly. I imagine there is a bug in the code that \"renormalizes\" mesh normals.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open the attached project/scene.\n- Select the `mesh` node.\n- Slide its `xy` value in the inspector until the normals \"pop\".\n- Note that this is also possible to reproduce if the node's `Rotation Edit Mode` is set to `Euler`, by scaling it along the Z axis only. But the popping effect in that case is a little more subtle.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18369321/bug-report.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101377/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}